# Keep text files LF in the working tree, not just in the object store.
#
# Without this, a checkout on Windows rewrites these files with CRLF, and every
# test that pins a multi-line SQL or source fragment with "\n" fails — six of
# them did, on a tree that had passed moments earlier, purely because a branch
# switch re-materialised the files. That is a false failure that looks exactly
# like a real regression, on the files where a real regression matters most.
#
# The tests also normalise line endings when they read, so the suite is robust
# either way; this stops the churn at the source.
#
# NOTE: this attribute only takes effect when a file is (re-)materialised. Files
# that were already checked out before the rule landed keep their CRLF endings
# until something rewrites them; see README "Verification" for how to check.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Extension-less binaries live here too — a blanket CRLF→LF sweep silently
# corrupted this WebP by one byte before it was marked.
.thumbnail binary

*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
# The frozen worklist's gzip copies (R6, November 7, 2026) are binary.
worklist.json.gz binary
worklist.md.gz binary
